---
import:
  - personality
description: Shared domain concepts for the dental voice receptionist project — used by both the Next.js web module and the Python LiveKit voice agent module.
---

***definitions***
- :Patient: is a person who calls the practice through the call simulator to ask about services, hours, staff, or to book an appointment.
- :PracticeAdmin: is a person at the dental practice who uses the web admin UI to configure the practice (services, staff, working hours, greeting). The MVP has exactly one :PracticeAdmin: and no authentication.
- :Staff: is a dentist or hygienist employed by the practice. :Staff: members are entered and edited by :PracticeAdmin:, do not log in themselves, and are referenced by the voice agent when discussing availability and booking appointments with :Patient:. :Staff: has:
  - Name - the staff member's full name as the agent should say it (required, non-empty)
  - Role - a short job title such as "Dentist" or "Hygienist" (required, non-empty)
  - Bio - a short English description the agent may read when the :Patient: asks about a specific staff member (optional)
- :Practice: is the dental practice that the system serves. Exactly one :Practice: exists in the MVP. :Practice: has:
  - Name - the public-facing name of the practice (required, non-empty)
  - Address - a free-form street address (required, non-empty)
  - PhoneDisplay - the phone number the agent reads aloud when the :Patient: asks for it (required, non-empty)
  - HoursOfOperation - a weekly recurring schedule of when the practice is open, with one entry per day of week that has open hours (each entry: day of week from Monday..Sunday, open time, close time)
  - GreetingStyle - a :GreetingStyle: value selecting the opening line format the agent uses (required; default: `warm`)
  - CustomGreeting - a free-text override used verbatim when GreetingStyle is `custom` (optional)
  - ToneProfile - a :ToneProfile: value controlling the agent's register throughout calls (required; default: `friendly`)
  - ClosingStyle - a :ClosingStyle: value selecting the closing line format the agent uses (required; default: `standard`)
  - CustomClosing - a free-text override used verbatim when ClosingStyle is `custom` (optional)
  - AgentGender - a :AgentGender: value selecting the ElevenLabs voice preset (optional; default: `female`)
  - AgentName - the name the agent uses to introduce itself at the start of a call, e.g. "Alex" or "Maya" (optional; if unset the agent does not introduce itself by name)
- :Service: is something the :Practice: offers to a :Patient:, such as a cleaning, a filling, or a checkup. :Service: has:
  - Name - the public name of the service (required, non-empty)
  - DurationMinutes - how long the service takes, as a positive integer multiple of 15 (required)
  - PriceCents - the price of the service in US-dollar cents, as a non-negative integer (required)
  - Description - one or two sentences in English describing what the service is, read by the voice agent when the :Patient: asks (required, non-empty)
  - Category - a short label grouping this service with similar ones, e.g. "Preventive", "Cosmetic", "Restorative", "Emergency" (optional; if unset the service is uncategorised)
  - PreProcedureInstructions - one or two English sentences the agent reads to the :Patient: when confirming a booking, describing what to do or avoid before the appointment (optional; pre-filled with standard best practices in the demo seed; editable by :PracticeAdmin:)
  - PostProcedureInstructions - one or two English sentences the agent reads to the :Patient: when confirming a booking, describing aftercare guidance (optional; pre-filled with standard best practices in the demo seed; editable by :PracticeAdmin:)
- :WorkingHours: is a single recurring weekly time window during which a specific :Staff: member is available for appointments. A :Staff: member can have many :WorkingHours: entries (for example, one for each weekday morning and one for each weekday afternoon). :WorkingHours: has:
  - StaffRef - the :Staff: member these hours belong to (required)
  - DayOfWeek - one of Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday (required)
  - StartTime - the start time on that day, expressed as HH:MM in 24-hour local clock and aligned to a quarter-hour mark (00, 15, 30, or 45 minutes) (required)
  - EndTime - the end time on that day, also HH:MM 24-hour aligned to a quarter-hour mark, strictly later than StartTime (required)
- :Appointment: is a confirmed booking made by a :Patient: with a specific :Staff: member for a specific :Service: at a specific date and time. :Appointment: has:
  - PatientPhone - the phone number of the :Patient:, captured from the call simulator at the start of the call (required, non-empty)
  - PatientName - the first and last name of the :Patient: as the patient stated it during the call (required, non-empty)
  - StaffRef - the :Staff: member who will provide the service (required)
  - ServiceRef - the :Service: being booked (required)
  - StartAt - the local date and time when the appointment begins, aligned to a quarter-hour mark (00, 15, 30, or 45 minutes past the hour) (required)
  - EndAt - the local date and time when the appointment ends, equal to StartAt plus the DurationMinutes of the referenced :Service: (required, derived)
  - Status - either "booked" or "cancelled"; in the MVP only "booked" is used and is the default (required)
  - CreatedAt - the timestamp when the appointment record was created (required)
  - Validity - an :Appointment: is valid only if it falls entirely within at least one :WorkingHours: entry of its StaffRef on the matching DayOfWeek and does not overlap any other :Appointment: of the same StaffRef whose Status is "booked"
- :Call: is the persistent record of one simulated phone call between a :Patient: and the voice agent. :Call: has:
  - PatientPhone - the phone number entered by the :Patient: in the call simulator at the start of the call (required, non-empty)
  - StartedAt - the timestamp when the agent joined the room and the conversation began (required)
  - EndedAt - the timestamp when the call was hung up by either side (optional while the call is in progress, required once the call has ended)
  - Status - one of "in_progress" or "ended" (required)
  - Transcript - the full back-and-forth between :Patient: and the voice agent, in chronological order, with each line labelled by speaker (required, may be empty while the call has just started)
  - Summary - a short English summary of the call written at the end of the call by the voice agent (optional, present only when Status is "ended")
  - AppointmentRef - the :Appointment: that was created during this call, if any (optional)
  - Outcome - one of "resolved" (the :Patient:'s questions were answered and/or a booking was completed with no outstanding items), "needs_callback" (the agent explicitly promised a staff member would call the :Patient: back), or "needs_action" (some other item requires staff follow-up). Present only when Status is "ended"; optional while the call is in progress.
- :StaffTask: is an actionable item created during or after a :Call: that requires follow-up by :PracticeAdmin: or another staff member. :StaffTask: has:
  - CallRef - the :Call: this task was generated from (required)
  - PatientPhone - copied from the :Call: for quick reference (required, non-empty)
  - PatientName - the name the :Patient: stated during the :Call:, if they gave one; empty string if the patient did not identify themselves (optional; defaults to empty string)
  - Description - a plain English sentence describing what action is needed (required, non-empty)
  - Topic - a short label (two to four words) classifying the conversation topic, generated by the voice agent at task-creation time; e.g. "General question", "Rescheduling", "Feedback", "Insurance inquiry", "Clinical question", "Appointment inquiry", "Pricing question" (optional; defaults to empty string if unset)
  - Type - one of "callback" (a staff member should call the patient back) or "action" (some other staff action is needed, e.g. an insurance question or a clinical referral) (required; default "callback")
  - Priority - one of "normal" or "high"; "high" is used when the :Patient: expressed urgency during the :Call: (required; default "normal")
  - Status - one of "open" (not yet handled) or "done" (handled by staff) (required; default "open")
  - CreatedAt - the server timestamp when the task was created (required)
  - ResolvedAt - the server timestamp when the task was marked "done" (optional; absent while open)
